{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QDEyYAeyyNiRAZUpXjZXDJ","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (50.8KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/d383f58c-515d-419c-8755-8a8284587d1d/tool-results/bscqb4k77.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D18 seen vs. D19+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-18 after D18 (1194 ids, 132 members; D18 added Google Apps Script `.gs` + a `google_docs_sidebar` host in a NEW\nmulti-line `SPLIT` carrier; single CORRECT T+54 s after a solve.py carrier patch, TT/Mastery first try). Every queued prebuild\ngap through D18 is built (only python-exec-onion-static given up); the queue below is new. Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SP