{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011EU9RXL4okw84snZM1LDK9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D18 seen vs. D19+ candidates)\n2\t\n3\tUpdated 2026-10-18 after D18 (1194 ids, 132 members; D18 added Google Apps Script `.gs` + a `google_docs_sidebar` host in a NEW\n4\tmulti-line `SPLIT` carrier; single CORRECT T+54 s after a solve.py carrier patch, TT/Mastery first try). Every queued prebuild\n5\tgap through D18 is built (only python-exec-onion-static given up); the queue below is new. Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\n6\tactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\n7\thave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n8\t\n9\tContext that drives the likelihood column:\n10\t- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n11\t  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n12\t  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n13\t  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n14\t  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n15\t  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n16\t  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n17\t  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n18\t  D18 solve.py; `lib.codec.v3_plan` still returns None -> gap v3-split-array-carrier). The real D19+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n19\t  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n20\t  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n21\t  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n22\t  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n23\t  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n24\t  -- yet. D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n25\t  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n26\t  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n27\t- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n28\t  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host). D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n29\t  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n30\t  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n31\t  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: fake \"Decrypt document\" lure). Languages still\n32\t  unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Office Scripts/Excel add-ins, Chrome extension JS, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F#\n33\t  scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker, Swift/JXA.\n34\t- ~13 drops left (D19-D31).\n35\t  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n36\t  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n37\t  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n38\t  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n39\t  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n40\t\n41\t## 1. Concept table\n42\t\n43\tLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\n44\tfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n45\t\n46\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n47\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n48\t| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n49\t| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n50\t| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n51\t| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n52\t| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n53\t| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n54\t| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n55\t| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/`$_REQUEST` | V3_MARK peel; `php` MISSING (`apt install php-cli` for `php -l`/token dump only) | carried daily |\n56\t| 9 | WSF / HTA hosts | seen D8 | `<job><script language=..>`, `<hta:application>`, mixed JScript+VBS | extract each `<script>` body (lxml/bs4 INSTALLED) and route by language | carried |\n57\t| 10 | Lua + OpenResty host | seen D9 | `local descriptor_`, `--` comments, `ngx.`, `inert_handler_<id>` | V3_MARK; `lua`/`luac` MISSING (`apt install lua5.4`) | carried |\n58\t| 11 | SCT scriptlet (regsvr32 /i:url scrobj.dll, Squiblydoo) | seen D9 (host) | `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>`, `<![CDATA[` | strip CDATA -> JScript/VBS route | carried |\n59\t| 12 | WMI MOF | seen D10 | `#pragma namespace`, `instance of __EventFilter`, `ActiveScriptEventConsumer`, `ScriptText =` | V3_MARK; ScriptText is a C-escaped JS/VBS string -> unescape then route | carried |\n60\t| 13 | TypeScript | seen D11 | type annotations, `interface`, `as const`, `.ts` | V3_