tLab CI          - hosts:/tasks: -> ansible\n140\t resource \"x\" / provisioner \"local-exec\" -> terraform    Windows Registry Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n141\t [Version] Signature=\"$CHICAGO$\" -> .inf   [InternetShortcut] -> .url   [Shell] Command= -> .scf\n142\t <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n143\t <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild    Installer + [RunInstaller(true)] -> InstallUtil C#\n144\t Sub AutoOpen/Document_Open/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA   =EXEC(/=FORMULA( in a sheet -> XLM\n145\t instance of __EventFilter -> MOF        #r \"nuget: -> csx   let/printfn/|> -> fsx   Deno./Bun. -> deno/bun\n146\tPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n147\t grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n148\t marker with NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n149\t   `<TAG>-`, peel (solve.py has it, lib.codec not yet); other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})`\n150\t   `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: fix the read, never walk role/attack enums.\n151\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n152\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n153\t material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n154\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n155\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n156\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n157\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\n158\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n159\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n160\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n161\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n162\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n163\t XLM .venv/bin/xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK .venv/bin/lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper x.exe out/, a3x\n164\t Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n165\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n166\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n167\tNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n168\t `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\n169\tSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n170\t `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15+); a carried label rejected\n171\t on unchanged bytes = GM regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh first.\n172\tEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16): only if asked; compare lib.codec.plan_canonical (role/steps/adapter/attack/profiles).\n173\tNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n174\t then lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes) (pcap/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon 3,22) + reconcile({member: plan}, bytes) -> reconcile_answer\n175\t (r, kind, accepted, what=). Graph ids: download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key suffix: plan_answer.\n176\tPROCESS-TREE prompt (D18 \"which process should spawn which ... child claiming a parent it never had\"): flavour unless asked.\n177\t Declared edge = file's host interpreter -> next_language interpreter (steps dispatch_process/dispatch_language) + spawn\n178\t call sites; observed = Sysmon EID1 ParentProcessGuid/ParentImage, 4688 creator pid, auditd ppid. Liar = child whose\n179\t recorded parent != declared parent (PPID spoofing T1134.004); match on GUID before pid (pid reuse), keep original spelling.\n180\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n181\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans so far used parent T1059.\n182\t```\n183\t\n184\t## Readiness gaps\n185\tBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16 night source-encoding-normalize, equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route; D17 night download-graph-model, network-evidence-reconcile, plan-key-passthrough, indicator-refang-normalize, ahk-compiled-exe-extract, vba-module-route, dockerfile-makefile-route; D18 night (before the D18 drop) network-evidence-indicators, source-fetch-sites, reconcile-indicator-kinds, http-redirect-dns-resolve, pcap-http-object-hashes, sysmon-proxy-log-fetches, ps-v3-polyglot-route, lolbin-download-attack-table, python-onion-regex-fold (all `lib.codec`; earlier: batch-substring-emulation, container-carrier-extract, descriptor-syntax-generic, gzip-zlib-codec-rep, php-eval-chain, ps-layer-peel, v3-peel-widen, xslt-msxsl-route). Given up: python-exec-onion-static (2 attempts, `import ast` banned). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no csv/ast/tokenize/shlex/marshal; dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile OK). Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D18 5-set Mastery 17.7 s). Priority-1 order for D19: the SPLIT carrier in lib (today's real miss), then the D18 process-tree pattern (router -> telemetry -> tree -> static tree -> reconcile).\n186\t\n187\t```json\n188\t[\n189\t  {\"id\": \"v3-split-array-carrier\", \"concept\": \"v=3 marker with no data + multi-line literal-array carrier (D18 SPLIT) in lib.codec\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs return None on all 5 D18 .gs files: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` has no data and the plan is `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\\\"FRAG-..\\\", \\\"..\\\", ..].join(\\\"\\\")` over ~16 lines (first chunk carries the real tag FRAG/HEX/HB64/B64), plus an untagged copy `const encoded_<id> = [..].join(\\\"\\\")` in buildAnalysisPlan_<id>(). The D18 solve.py fix: regex every all-literal array `\\\\[\\\\s*((?:(?:\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"|'[^']*'|`[^`$]*`)\\\\s*,?\\\\s*)+)\\\\]`, join, also try with `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-` stripped, peel, accept `v=`. Port it into lib.codec and generalise to the same layout in every carried host syntax: Python `\\\"\\\".join([..])` / tuple, PS `-join @(..)` / `[string]::Join('', @(..))`, Lua `table.concat({..})`, Perl `join('', (..))` / qw(), Ruby `[..].join` / %w[], VBS `Join(Array(..), \\\"\\\")`, AHK `[..]` + loop join, AutoIt `StringJoin`/`_ArrayToString`, AppleScript `{..} as text` with `text item delimiters`, MSBuild repeated `<Chunk>` elements, batch `set c1=..` runs. Gate: all D18 .gs members + a fixture battery of D17 plans re-wrapped in each syntax decode to the same plan; no regressions on D1-D18 bundles.\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"evidence-type-router\", \"concept\": \"classify any NON-script member (second evidence type) and dispatch to its reader\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt named network evidence, D18 native process telemetry; neither shipped yet, but the day it does the worker must know in one call what the extra file is. evidence_kind(name, bytes)->{kind: pcap|pcapng|har|zeek|sysmon_evtx|sysmon_xml|sysmon_json|security_4688|auditd|ps_listing|procmon_csv|w3c|squid|edr_json|unknown, reader: lib function name, records: n} by magic/shape (ElfFile header for EVTX, `<Events>`/`<Event xmlns=` XML, JSON lines with EventID/ProcessGuid/event.code, `type=SYSCALL`, `UID PID PPID C STIME`, `\\\"Time of Day\\\",\\\"Process Name\\\",\\\"PID\\\"` Procmon CSV). Then route: network -> network_indicators, process -> process_events (gap process-telemetry-windows/-linux-text), file/registry -> file_registry_events. Gate: every D1-D18 script member classifies as `script` (no false positives).\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"process-telemetry-windows\", \"concept\": \"observed process events from Sysmon EID 1/5 and Security 4688/4689 (EVTX, XML, JSON, text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 prompt: 'native telemetry keeps its own record of events'. process_events(data, name='')->[{ts, pid, ppid, image, cmdline, parent_image, parent_cmdline, guid, parent_guid, user, integrity, hashes, event:start|end, src}] from Sysmon EID 1 (ProcessId, ProcessGuid, ParentProcessId, ParentProcessGuid, ParentImage, ParentCommandLine, CommandLine, Image), EID 5 (terminate), Security 4688 (NewProcessId hex, NewProcessName, ProcessId = CREATOR pid hex, ParentProcessName, CommandLine) and 4689; inputs EVTX (Evtx lib allowed), exported XML, winlogbeat/ECS JSON (process.pid/process.parent.pid/process.entity_id), Splunk-style key=value text. Hex pids (`0x1a2c`) -> int; keep the original spelling for answers. Reuse the _ni_sysmon/_ni_evtx plumbing. No csv module (gate).\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"process-tree-model\", \"concept\": \"build the observed process tree; roots, orphans, depth, chain, pid reuse\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Depends on process-telemetry-windows. process_tree(events)->{nodes, edges, roots, orphans (parent pid/guid never seen or exited before the child started), chains(leaf)->[root..leaf], depth, children(node)} keyed by ProcessGuid when present, else (pid, start ts) so pid reuse does not merge two processes; a 4688 creator pid resolved to the process alive at that time. process_tree_answer(tree, kind, accepted_values, what=) for root/leaf/parent-of/children-of/depth/count/orphan questions, image basenames compared case-insensitively but answered in original spelling. The title 'Orphan Process' = parent missing from the log.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"static-process-tree\", \"concept\": \"declared (static) process tree from source + plan\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 prompt: 'Source code describes which process should spawn which ... reconstruct the static process tree'. declared_spawns(plans_by_member, sources)->[{member, parent_image, child_image, cmdline, api, line}]: parent = the member's host interpreter (lang/host_profile -> wscript.exe|cscript.exe for jscript/vbscript/wsf, mshta.exe for hta, cmd.exe for batch, powershell.exe/pwsh.exe, python.exe, node.exe, perl, ruby, lua, AutoHotkey64.exe, AutoIt3.exe, osascript, msbuild.exe, regsvr32.exe for sct, WmiPrvSE.exe/scrcons.exe for MOF, bash), child = next_language interpreter when steps contain dispatch_process/dispatch_language/handoff_script, plus code call sites (WScript.Shell Run/Exec, Shell.Application ShellExecute, Start-Process/&/Invoke-Expression, cmd /c, start, child_process spawn/exec/fork, subprocess/os.system, system/qx/backticks, Ruby spawn/%x, AHK/AutoIt Run, do shell script, Win32_Process.Create, schtasks /create /tr, wmic process call create) with args rebuilt via the fetch_sites literal folder. Gate: every D18 v=3 member yields its edge consistent with its plan.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"process-tree-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"declared vs observed process tree; the child claiming a parent it never had\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Depends on static-process-tree + process-tree-model. reconcile_processes(declared, observed)->{matched, parent_mismatch: [{child, declared_parent, recorded_parent, real_parent_if_known, pid, guid}], declared_only (never ran), observed_only (unexpected child), orphans}; match child by image basename + cmdline canon (gap cmdline-canon) + time order; flag PPID spoofing when the recorded ParentProcessId/ParentImage differs from the declared parent or from the process that actually created it (Sysmon EID 1 ParentProcessGuid vs 4688 creator pid, or CreatorProcessId field). reconcile_processes_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=) -> child image / pid / claimed parent / true parent / count / ATT&CK (T1134.004).\"},\n195\t  {\"id\": \"spawn-api-parent-table\", \"concept\": \"which parent telemetry records for each spawn API (proxy parents) + ATT&CK\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Data table in lib.scripts used by static-process-tree/process-tree-reconcile so an 'unexpected' parent is not mis-flagged: WMI Win32_Process.Create / wmic process call create -> WmiPrvSE.exe (T1047); schtasks/Register-ScheduledTask -> svchost.exe (Schedule) / taskeng.exe (T1053.005); COM MMC20.Application -> mmc.exe, ShellWindows/ShellBrowserWindow -> explorer.exe (T1559.001/T1021.003); services sc create -> services.exe (T1543.003); WMI event consumer -> scrcons.exe (T1546.003); Run keys -> explorer.exe/userinit.exe; Outlook/Office macros -> WINWORD.EXE/EXCEL.EXE (T1204.002); mshta/regsvr32/rundll32 hosts; Apps Script/cloud = no local process. PPID-spoof code cues: UpdateProcThreadAttribute + PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS (0x00020000), STARTUPINFOEX, EXTENDED_STARTUPINFO_PRESENT (0x00080000), OpenProcess(PROCESS_CREATE_PROCESS 0x0080) on explorer.exe/svchost.exe, PS Get-Process explorer | ... CreateProcess -> T1134.004. Return candidates in order; plan attack= still wins.\"},\n196\t  {\"id\": \"process-telemetry-linux-text\", \"concept\": \"observed process events from auditd / ps forests / osquery / Sysmon-for-Linux / Procmon CSV\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Same record shape as process-telemetry-windows. auditd: group `type=SYSCALL ... syscall=59 ppid= pid= exe=` with `type=EXECVE argc= a0=` (hex-encoded args decode) and `type=PROCTITLE proctitle=<hex NUL-joined>` by msg=audit(ts:serial); `ps -ef` / `ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd` / `ps auxf` ASCII forest (`\\\\_` indentation = parent); osquery process_events JSON; Sysmon-for-Linux XML (EID 1 same fields); Procmon CSV `Process Create` rows (Detail `PID: n, Command line:`) and pstree text. Hand-split CSV with a quote-aware regex (no csv module).\"},\n197\t  {\"id\": \"cmdline-canon\", \"concept\": \"canonical command lines for matching declared vs observed spawns\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"canon_cmdline(s)->str: strip outer quotes, collapse whitespace, lower-case the image basename (keep args case), drop `.exe`, resolve `%COMSPEC%`/`%SystemRoot%`/`$env:` with the lib.codec _PS_ENV table, remove cmd `^` carets and `\\\"\\\"`, normalise `/c` vs `/C`, `-EncodedCommand`/`-enc`/`-e` -> decoded UTF-16LE text, `C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\` vs `C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\system32\\\\` vs 8.3 `PROGRA~1`, forward/back slashes; split_cmdline(s) Windows (CommandLineToArgvW rules) and POSIX quoting without shlex (gate). Used by process-tree-reconcile and by fetch-site matching.\"},\n198\t  {\"id\": \"file-registry-telemetry-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"declared file/registry/schedule indicators vs file/registry/task telemetry\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The daily second-evidence rotation went network (D17) -> process (D18); file and registry are the obvious next. file_registry_events(data)->[{ts, kind: file_create|file_delete|reg_set|reg_create|task_create|service_install, path, value, details, image, pid}] from Sysmon EID 11/23/26 (TargetFilename), 12/13/14 (TargetObject, Details), Security 4698/4702 (TaskContent XML), System 7045 (ServiceName/ImagePath), auditd PATH records, MFT/USN CSV text. reconcile_artifacts(plans, events) compares plan file_path/next_stage/cron_path/schedule_path/service_name/registry keys (canon: HKLM\\\\ vs HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\ vs \\\\REGISTRY\\\\MACHINE\\\\, case-insensitive Windows paths, %APPDATA% expansion) -> declared_only/observed_only/both + an answer helper like reconcile_answer.\"},\n199\t  {\"id\": \"saas-script-host-route\", \"concept\": \"cloud/SaaS and add-in script hosts after D18 Apps Script\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 opened SaaS hosts (google_docs_sidebar). Likely siblings: Apps Script `appsscript.json` manifest + .gs/.html pairs (sheets custom function, gmail add-on, web app doGet/doPost), Office Scripts `function main(workbook: ExcelScript.Workbook)` (.osts = JSON with the script in an escaped string `body`), Office JS add-in manifest.xml + taskpane.js, Chrome/Edge MV3 extension manifest.json + service_worker / content_scripts, Power Automate / Logic Apps definition JSON, Salesforce Apex `.cls`, VS Code extension package.json activationEvents. saas_host(name, src)->{profile guess, script texts}: unescape JSON-string-embedded code, follow manifest references inside the same zip, then the normal marker/descriptor/split-array readers. Gate: D18 .gs files still route; fixture battery of a D18 plan wrapped in each container.\"},\n200\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n201\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n202\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n203\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n204\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n205\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n206\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n207\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n208\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n209\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n210\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n211\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar).\"}\n212\t]\n213\t```\n214\tscript-analysis:ahk-compiled-exe-extract True 1\n215\tscript-analysis:batch-expansion-regime-lib True 1"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d383f58c-515d-419c-8755-8a8284587d1d","uuid":"153a2f62-5c26-4419-8e6d-a4aa03ce1e4d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:03:52.736Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/d383f58c-515d-419c-8755-8a8284587d1d/tool-results/bscqb4k77.txt","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D18 seen vs. D19+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-18 after D18 (1194 ids, 132 members; D18 added Google Apps Script `.gs` + a `google_docs_sidebar` host in a NEW\nmulti-line `SPLIT` carrier; single CORRECT T+54 s after a solve.py carrier patch, TT/Mastery first try). Every queued prebuild\ngap through D18 is built (only python-exec-onion-static given up); the queue below is new. Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n  D18 solve.py; `lib.codec.v3_plan` still returns None -> gap v3-split-array-carrier). The real D19+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n  -- yet. D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host). D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: fake \"Decrypt document\" lure). Languages still\n  unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Office Scripts/Excel add-ins, Chrome extension JS, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F#\n  scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker, Swift/JXA.\n- ~13 drops left (D19-D31).\n  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n\n## 1. Concept table\n\nLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\nfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/`$_REQUEST` | V3_MARK peel; `php` MISSING (`apt install php-cli` for `php -l`/token dump only) | carried daily |\n| 9 | WSF / HTA hosts | seen D8 | `<job><script language=..>`, `<hta:application>`, mixed JScript+VBS | extract each `<script>` body (lxml/bs4 INSTALLED) and route by language | carried |\n| 10 | Lua + OpenResty host | seen D9 | `local descriptor_`, `--` comments, `ngx.`, `inert_handler_<id>` | V3_MARK; `lua`/`luac` MISSING (`apt install lua5.4`) | carried |\n| 11 | SCT scriptlet (regsvr32 /i:url scrobj.dll, Squiblydoo) | seen D9 (host) | `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>`, `<![CDATA[` | strip CDATA -> JScript/VBS route | carried |\n| 12 | WMI MOF | seen D10 | `#pragma namespace`, `instance of __EventFilter`, `ActiveScriptEventConsumer`, `ScriptText =` | V3_MARK; ScriptText is a C-escaped JS/VBS string -> unescape then route | carried |\n| 13 | TypeScript | seen D11 | type annotations, `interface`, `as const`, `.ts` | V3_MARK; no tsc needed (strip types or read literals) | carried |\n| 14 | AutoIt `.au3` | seen D12 | `Global Const $descriptor_`, `;` comments, `#include <..>`, `Execute(`, `BinaryToString` | V3_MARK; compiled: `autoit-ripper x.exe out/` / `.venv/bin/a3x < x.a3x` (INSTALLED) | carried; compiled a3x = med |\n| 15 | AppleScript (source) | seen D13 | `property descriptor_<id> :`, `--` comments, `do shell script`, `osascript -e` | V3_MARK; compiled `.scpt` (`FasdUAS` magic) = no decompiler (MISSING: applescript-disassembler) | carried; `.scpt` = low/med |\n| 16 | MSBuild `.proj` inline task | seen D14 | `<Project xmlns=..msbuild..>`, `<UsingTask TaskFactory=\"CodeTaskFactory\">`, `<Code Type=\"Fragment\">` C# CDATA, `<HuntressDescriptor>` | V3_MARK in `<!-- -->`; lxml for the property element | carried |\n| 17 | Perl `.pl` + perl_cgi host | seen D15 | `#!/usr/bin/env perl`, `use strict;`, `my $descriptor_`, `print \"Content-Type:` | V3_MARK; `perl -MO=Deparse f.pl` (INSTALLED, parse-only, BEGIN blocks still run - strip them) | carried |\n| 18 | Ruby `.rb` (+ Rack host) | seen D16 | `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase const), `require`, `def ..end`, `def build_plan_<id>` returning `{ descriptor: DESCRIPTOR_<ID> }`, host `ruby_rack` = `INERT_RACK_<ID> = ->(_env) { [200, {..}, [..]] }` lambda | V3_MARK (carried solver, unchanged); `ruby -c f.rb` syntax only; ERB/Rails `<%= %>` hosts still unseen | carried |\n| 67 | AutoHotkey `.ahk` (v2) | seen D17 | `#Requires AutoHotkey v2.0`, `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..`, `descriptor_<8hex> := \"..\"`, `buildPlan_<id>() { global ..; return Map(\"descriptor\", ..) }`; v1 legacy would be `x = text` unquoted + `%x%` derefs + `( .. )` continuation sections | V3_MARK (carried solver, unchanged); compiled Ahk2Exe PE = RT_RCDATA `>AUTOHOTKEY SCRIPT<` -> lib.codec carrier walk (built D17 night, also AHK v1 `x = text` / continuation sections) | carried; compiled exe / v1 syntax = low/med |\n| 19 | PowerShell module / `.psm1` `.psd1` `.ps1xml` (v=3 polyglot-powershell) | gap (PS only v=1) | `Export-ModuleMember`, `FunctionsToExport`, `<Types><Type><ScriptMethod><Script>`, `<#  #>` block comments (marker may sit inside `<# #>`) | `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.psm1`; lxml for ps1xml `<Script>` nodes | **high**: PS is the canonical malware language and has no v=3 fixture |\n| 20 | Tcl / Expect | gap | `#!/usr/bin/tclsh`, `set descriptor_x \"...\"` (no `=`!), `proc`, `puts`, `binary decode base64`, `{braces}` strings | `tclsh` MISSING (`apt install tcl`); static: regex `set\\s+descriptor_\\w+\\s+[\"{]` | med |\n| 21 | R script | gap | `<-` assignment, `library(`, `base64enc::`, `rawToChar(`, `system(`, `#` comments | `Rscript` MISSING (`apt install r-base-core`, big); static `<-` descriptor regex | low/med |\n| 22 | Groovy / Jenkinsfile | gap | `pipeline { agent .. stages`, `sh '''..'''`, `def x = \"..\"`, `\"cmd\".execute()`, `.decodeBase64()` | `groovy` MISSING (java INSTALLED; jar from apache); static read | med: CI-abuse host fits \"trusted toolchain\" theme |\n| 23 | Kotlin script `.kts` / Gradle `build.gradle.kts` | gap | `val descriptor_x = \"..\"`, `plugins {`, `tasks.register`, `Runtime.getRuntime().exec`, `Base64.getDecoder()` | `kotlinc` MISSING; static | med (Gradle build abuse) |\n| 24 | Go (`go run`, `//go:generate`) | gap | `package main`, `descriptor_x := \"..\"` (`:=` breaks current regex), `exec.Command`, raw `` `..` `` strings | `go vet f.go` (INSTALLED /usr/bin/go; never `go run`) | med |\n| 25 | Rust script / `build.rs` | gap | `fn main()`, `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \"..\"`, `std::process::Command`, `r#\"..\"#` raw strings, `\\u{..}` | `rustc` INSTALLED (don't build); static | low/med (`build.rs` = build-time abuse) |\n| 26 | AWK program | gap | `BEGIN {`, `system(`, `\"cmd\" \\| getline`, `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` | `gawk --lint -f f.awk /dev/null` is NOT safe (BEGIN runs) -> static only | med (LOLBin `awk`, GTFOBins) |\n| 27 | sed script | gap | `#!/bin/sed -f`, `s/../../e` (GNU exec flag), `w /path` | static | low |\n| 28 | Makefile | gap | `target: deps` + TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)`, `DESCRIPTOR := ..` (`:=`), `.PHONY` | lib.codec Makefile route (built D17 night: `\\` joins, `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, `#` marker); never `make -n` (evaluates `$(shell)`) | med (build-system abuse theme) |\n| 29 | Dockerfile | gap | `FROM`, `RUN curl .. \\| sh`, `ENV`, `ARG`, `# HUNTRESS..` comments, `COPY --chmod` | lib.codec Dockerfile route (built D17 night: `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=`, `RUN echo .. \\| base64 -d`); never `docker build` | med |\n| 30 | CI YAML (GitHub Actions / GitLab CI) | gap | `on: [push]`, `jobs:`, `runs-on:`, `steps: - run:` + block scalar, `stages:`, `script:`; block scalars span lines | `.venv/bin/python -c 'import yaml,sys;print(yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1])))' f.yml` (INSTALLED); `yq` MISSING | med/high: supply-chain host, family would be `polyglot-github_actions`-style |\n| 31 | Ansible playbook | gap | `- hosts:`, `tasks:`, `ansible.builtin.shell:`, `become: true`, `vars:` | yaml.safe_load (INSTALLED); ansible MISSING (not needed) | low/med |\n| 32 | Terraform HCL | gap | `resource \"null_resource\"`, `provisioner \"local-exec\" { command = ..}`, `data \"external\"`, `locals {` | `terraform fmt -check` (INSTALLED; never init/plan); python-hcl2 MISSING | low/med |\n| 33 | XSL/XSLT via `msxsl.exe` / `wmic /format:` (Squiblytwo) | gap | `<xsl:stylesheet`, `xmlns:msxsl=\"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xslt\"`, `<msxsl:script language=\"JScript\" implements-prefix=..>` CDATA | lxml parse (INSTALLED), pull `msxsl:script` text -> JS/VBS route; NEVER apply the transform; `xsltproc` MISSING | **high**: Windows trusted-host abuse, sibling of D9 SCT / D14 MSBuild |\n| 34 | InstallUtil (.NET `[RunInstaller(true)]` C#) | gap | `System.Configuration.Install.Installer`, `Uninstall(IDictionary)` override, `/U` | read C#; compiled: `ilspycmd x.dll` (INSTALLED) | med (LOLBin family 