{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AtoDosaQCN7coRHJQZ5Yz6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n7\t  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n8\t  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n9\t  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n10\t  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl\n11\t  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members) -> +AutoHotkey `.ahk` (d17, 1139; 127\n12\t  members, no host file, no new Bash) -> +Google Apps Script `.gs` + `google_docs_sidebar` host (d18, 1194; 132 members, no new\n13\t  Bash) -> +Roslyn C# script `.csx` + `aspx_inline_csharp` host (d19, 1249; 137 members, no new Bash). Most days also add 2\n14\t  Bash advanced fixtures (not d12, d15, d17-d19). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up\n15\t  only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D17 \"Fetch Quest\" -> AutoHotkey; D18 \"Orphan Process\" ->\n16\t  Apps Script; D19 \"Sharp Practice\" / base `managed-assembly-bridge` -> C#). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.\n17\t- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n18\t  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n19\t  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n20\t  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n21\t- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n22\t  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n23\t- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,\n24\t  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks\n25\t  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n26\t- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly\n27\t  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n28\t  evidence ... the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"native telemetry keeps its own record ... reconstruct the static process\n29\t  tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\", D19 \"work out where the bridge actually leads\" = just the per-file\n30\t  `next-language` id) have NEVER been asked as a question. Neither D17's network evidence nor D18's process telemetry was in the zip. Answer the contract ids only; if such a file ever ships, see Recognition cues.\n31\t- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475\n32\t  ids), d17 (5695), d18 (5970), d19 (6245)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one\n33\t  `evidence-01.zip` holding every `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n34\t  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n35\t\n36\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\n37\tEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\n38\tMastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict; D17: no axis --\n39\tTT c474d1d8 and Mastery 65cb0a01 CORRECT first try, 0 VARIANT AXIS lines, `novel_labels: {}`; D18: no axis either -- TT\n40\t9bf550a3 11.7 s, Mastery 4d9ad8d7 17.7 s, first try; the day's only new shape was the SPLIT carrier, same in every mode;\n41\tD19: no axis -- TT e3b3b2d1 5.3 s, Mastery 42610860 12.2 s first try, 0 new VARIANT AXIS lines; the ESCAPED-NESTED ASPX carrier\n42\twas the same shape in every mode).\n43\t- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n44\t  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n45\t  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; D16+ every mode incl. the single): label the JOIN\n46\t  STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool; bare `call set\n47\t  \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent.\n48\t  Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.\n49\t  label_regime`/`label_expansion`); old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different\n50\t  labels, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) at once.\n51\t- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n52\t  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n53\t  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n54\t  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n55\t- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n56\t  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n57\t- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n58\t  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D17, only\n59\t  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n60\t  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n61\t  **D18 `SPLIT` is a LAYOUT tag, not an encoding**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` stands alone on its line and the data is the\n62\t  next multi-line literal array `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\"<TAG>-chunk\", \"chunk\", ..].join(\"\")`; the real tag\n63\t  (FRAG/HEX/HB64/B64) is the first chunk's prefix, and `buildAnalysisPlan_<id>()` holds an untagged copy (`const encoded_<id> =\n64\t  [..].join(\"\")`). Parse rule: if the marker match has no data, join every all-literal array / concat run in the file\n65\t  (quotes `\"` `'` and backticks), strip a leading `[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-`, peel; keep the one that yields `v=`. Patched in the\n66\t  D18 solve.py (`_v3` candidates); lib.codec.v3_plan handles it since the D18-night prebuild.\n67\t- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF ScriptText, D19 ASPX)** -- the whole inner script is a string literal of the host:\n68\t  `<%@ Page Language=\"C#\" %><script runat=\"server\"> private static readonly string EmbeddedCsx_<8hex> = \"// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:\n69\t  HEX-<data>\\n#nullable enable\\n..string descriptor_<id> = \\\"<data>\\\";\\n\";`. In raw bytes the marker data runs on into a\n70\t  literal `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is `\\\"`-quoted, so the carried regexes find nothing. Parse rule: when a v=3 file\n71\t  yields no plan, unescape string-literal escapes (`\\n \\\" \\\\ \\t`, C# verbatim `\"\"`, VB `\"\"`, XML `&quot;`/CDATA, JSON\n72\t  `\\u0022`) and rescan; or stop marker data at `\\`. `lib.codec.v3_plan` already decoded the D19 ASPX file at solve time\n73\t  (the carried solve.py did not call it) -- **fall back to lib.codec.v3_plan before anything else**.\n74\t- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n75\t  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt, AutoHotkey), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n76\t  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n77\t  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16),\n78\t  **`descriptor_<8hex> := \"..\"` AutoHotkey v2 (D17)**, C# `string descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";` + `BuildPlan_<id>() => new\n79\t  Dictionary<string,string> { [\"descriptor\"] = .. }` (D19), Apps Script `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` +\n80\t  `Object.freeze({ descriptor: encoded_<id> })` (D18). Never anchor on `=` / `:=` / `set` / `<-` -- parse rule: regex\n81\t  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, any comment syntax/case/extension; if the data group\n82\t  is empty (`SPLIT`), fall through to the literal-array join above.\n83\t- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix: decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read by `parseInt(x, R)`/`int(x, R)` --\n84\t  READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE (keys too); base64 standard AND urlsafe (whitelist + pad); reversal of the LIST\n85\t  (`reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list`) vs the TEXT (`reversed_base64`) -- try both; material as one literal, split chunks,\n86\t  `+=`, adjacent strings, `.`-FRAG, D18 multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` -- join first; same-language carrier may be a frozen exe (D6\n87\t  cx_Freeze) -- locate by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), never by file type.\n88\t- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n89\t  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n90\t- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n91\t  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local\n92\t  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted); D17 Mastery (5 sets, 5695 ids) CORRECT in 12.7 s (start\n93\t  4.1, download 0.7, solve 5.6, submit 2.3) and D18 Mastery (5970 ids) in 17.7 s (start 7.7, submit 7.4, solve 0.5) -- the cap\n94\t  problem is fixed; start+submit transport now dominates. None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n95\t\n96\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n97\t| You see | First move |\n98\t|---|---|\n99\t| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n100\t| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D17: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged; D18 and D19 each needed a CARRIER patch). Any file it leaves planless: try `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)` next (it had D19's fix already). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |\n101\t| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n102\t| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |\n103\t| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n104\t| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n105\t| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n106\t| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n107\t| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n108\t| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n109\t| Prompt about fetch targets vs \"network evidence\" / \"only one side\" (D17), but the zip holds only scripts | Flavour: answer the per-file ids. If a pcap/HAR/Zeek/proxy/DNS/Sysmon file ships: `obs = lib.codec.network_indicators(raw_bytes)` (pcap/pcapng/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon EID 3/22/W3C; `http_objects` reassembles bodies, `resolve_chain` follows redirects/CNAMEs), `r = lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, raw_bytes)` -> `reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=)` (urls/hosts/ips/user_agents/file_names `.observed_only`/`.declared_only`; answers keep the ORIGINAL spelling). Declared side from code: `lib.codec.fetch_sites(src)`. Graph questions (chain/root/leaf/unique/counts): `download_graph(plans)` + `download_graph_answer`. tshark (INSTALLED) = oracle only. |\n110\t| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (marker with NO data on its line) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [ \"FRAG-..\", \"..\", ..].join(\"\")` (D18 `.gs`) | Multi-line literal-array carrier. Join the array's literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head of chunk 1, peel as usual (lib.codec.v3_plan and the D18+ solve.py `_v3` loop both do). If the 44 new ids come back unanswered, fix the CARRIER read first -- never walk the role enum. |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d383f58c-515d-419c-8755-8a8284587d1d","uuid":"15f777df-f1a0-4f95-9968-3b44825948bb","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:05:28.386Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-19; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl\n  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members) -> +AutoHotkey `.ahk` (d17, 1139; 127\n  members, no host file, no new Bash) -> +Google Apps Script `.gs` + `google_docs_sidebar` host (d18, 1194; 132 members, no new\n  Bash) -> +Roslyn C# script `.csx` + `aspx_inline_csharp` host (d19, 1249; 137 members, no new Bash). Most days also add 2\n  Bash advanced fixtures (not d12, d15, d17-d19). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up\n  only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D17 \"Fetch Quest\" -> AutoHotkey; D18 \"Orphan Process\" ->\n  Apps Script; D19 \"Sharp Practice\" / base `managed-assembly-bridge` -> C#). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,\n  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks\n  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly\n  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence ... the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"native telemetry keeps its own record ... reconstruct the static process\n  tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\", D19 \"work out where the bridge actually leads\" = just the per-file\n  `next-language` id) have NEVER been asked as a question. Neither D17's network evidence nor D18's process telemetry was in the zip. Answer the contract ids only; if such a file ever ships, see Recognition cues.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475\n  ids), d17 (5695), d18 (5970), d19 (6245)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one\n  `evidence-01.zip` holding every `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\nMastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict; D17: no axis --\nTT c474d1d8 and Mastery 65cb0a01 CORRECT first try, 0 VARIANT AXIS lines, `novel_labels: {}`; D18: no axis either -- TT\n9bf550a3 11.7 s, Mastery 4d9ad8d7 17.7 s, first try; the day's only new shape was the SPLIT carrier, same in every mode;\nD19: no axis -- TT e3b3b2d1 5.3 s, Mastery 42610860 12.2 s first try, 0 new VARIANT AXIS lines; the ESCAPED-NESTED ASPX carrier\nwas the same shape in every mode).\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; D16+ every mode incl. the single): label the JOIN\n  STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool; bare `call set\n  \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent.\n  Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.\n  label_regime`/`label_expansion`); old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different\n  labels, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) at once.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D17, only\n  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n  **D18 `SPLIT` is a LAYOUT tag, not an encoding**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` stands alone on its line and the data is the\n  next multi-line literal array `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\"<TAG>-chunk\", \"chunk\", ..].join(\"\")`; the real tag\n  (FRAG/HEX/HB64/B64) is the first chunk's prefix, and `buildAnalysisPlan_<id>()` holds an untagged copy (`const encoded_<id> =\n  [..].join(\"\")`). Parse rule: if the marker match has no data, join every all-literal array / concat run in the file\n  (quotes `\"` `'` and backticks), strip a leading `[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-`, peel; keep the one that yields `v=`. Patched in the\n  D18 solve.py (`_v3` candidates); lib.codec.v3_plan handles it since the D18-night prebuild.\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF ScriptText, D19 ASPX)** -- the whole inner script is a string literal of the host:\n  `<%@ Page Language=\"C#\" %><script runat=\"server\"> private static readonly string EmbeddedCsx_<8hex> = \"// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:\n  HEX-<data>\\n#nullable enable\\n..string descriptor_<id> = \\\"<data>\\\";\\n\";`. In raw bytes the marker data runs on into a\n  literal `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is `\\\"`-quoted, so the carried regexes find nothing. Parse rule: when a v=3 file\n  yields no plan, unescape string-literal escapes (`\\n \\\" \\\\ \\t`, C# verbatim `\"\"`, VB `\"\"`, XML `&quot;`/CDATA, JSON\n  `\\u0022`) and rescan; or stop marker data at `\\`. `lib.codec.v3_plan` already decoded the D19 ASPX file at solve time\n  (the carried solve.py did not call it) -- **fall back to lib.codec.v3_plan before anything else**.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt, AutoHotkey), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16),\n  **`descriptor_<8hex> := \"..\"` AutoHotkey v2 (D17)**, C# `string descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\";` + `BuildPlan_<id>() => new\n  Dictionary<string,string> { [\"descriptor\"] = .. }` (D19), Apps Script `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` +\n  `Object.freeze({ descriptor: encoded_<id> })` (D18). Never anchor on `=` / `:=` / `set` / `<-` -- parse rule: regex\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, any comment syntax/case/extension; if the data group\n  is empty (`SPLIT`), fall through to the literal-array join above.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix: decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read by `parseInt(x, R)`/`int(x, R)` --\n  READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE (keys too); base64 standard AND urlsafe (whitelist + pad); reversal of the LIST\n  (`reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list`) vs the TEXT (`reversed_base64`) -- try both; material as one literal, split chunks,\n  `+=`, adjacent strings, `.`-FRAG, D18 multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` -- join first; same-language carrier may be a frozen exe (D6\n  cx_Freeze) -- locate by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), never by file type.\n- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local\n  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted); D17 Mastery (5 sets, 5695 ids) CORRECT in 12.7 s (start\n  4.1, download 0.7, solve 5.6, submit 2.3) and D18 Mastery (5970 ids) in 17.7 s (start 7.7, submit 7.4, solve 0.5) -- the cap\n  problem is fixed; start+submit transport now dominates. None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D17: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged; D18 and D19 each needed a CARRIER patch). Any file it leaves planless: try `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)` next (it had D19's fix already). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs \"network evidence\" / \"only one side\" (D17), but the zip holds only scripts | Flavour: answer the per-file ids. If a pcap/HAR/Zeek/proxy/DNS/Sysmon file ships: `obs = lib.codec.network_indicators(raw_bytes)` (pcap/pcapng/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon EID 3/22/W3C; `http_objects` reassembles bodies, `resolve_chain` follows redirects/CNAMEs), `r = lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, raw_bytes)` -> `reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=)` (urls/hosts/ips/user_agents/file_names `.observed_only`/`.declared_only`; answers keep the ORIGINAL spelling). Declared side from code: `lib.codec.fetch_sites(src)`. Graph questions (chain/root/leaf/unique/counts): `download_graph(plans)` + `download_graph_answer`. tshark (INSTALLED) = oracle only. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (marker with NO data on its line) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [ \"FRAG-..\", \"..\", ..].join(\"\")` (D18 `.gs`) | Multi-line literal-array carrier. Join the array's literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head of chunk 1, peel as usual (lib.codec.v3_plan and the D18+ solve.py `_v3` loop both do). If the 44 new ids come back unanswered, fix the CARRIER read first -- never walk the role enum. |","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":247}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AtoDosaQCN7coRHJQZ5Yz6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","rea