e_handoff), next_language.\n175:- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, every host) and `T1053`\n176:  (persistence_descriptor); AutoHotkey (D17) too, not `.010`; Apps Script (D18) too, not `.007`; C# script (D19). The attack\n177:  question TEXT explains it: \"the parent Command and Scripting Interpreter technique is also accepted when a language-specific\n178:  sub-technique is canonical; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none is\n179:  also accepted for a relay\" -- read the question's precedence text before probing ATT&CK. **v=3 role does NOT follow\n180:  `steps`** (D14 MSBuild, D16 Ruby, D17 AHK benign_utility with `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`; D18 GAS benign_utility with\n181:  `decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process`, launcher with `decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role=,\n182:  steps=, stage_profile= independently.\n183:- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n184:  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n185:  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n186:  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n187:  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n188:  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n189:- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n190:  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n191:  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VB