-Path`. Then run v3_plan / find_codecs over every user string + resource. ilspycmd (INSTALLED) is the oracle only. Gate: synthetic minimal metadata blobs built in the fixture (no compiler), D1-D19 members classify as non-assembly.\"},\n {\"id\":\"managed-bridge-hosts\",\"concept\":\".NET-hosted script surfaces beyond ASPX/MSBuild: PS Add-Type C#, InstallUtil/RegAsm/RegSvcs, ashx/asmx/cshtml, classic ASP, Workflow Compiler XOML\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 host_profile spelling `aspx_inline_csharp` (<container>_<inline>_<lang>). managed_host(name, src)->{profile_guess, lang, inner_texts}: PowerShell `Add-Type -TypeDefinition @\\\"..\\\"@ [-Language CSharp]` / `-MemberDefinition` / `CSharpCodeProvider.CompileAssemblyFromSource(` / `[ScriptBlock]::Create`; `.ashx`/`.asmx` `<%@ WebHandler|WebService Language=\\\"C#\\\" Class=..%>` + code; Razor `.cshtml` `@{ .. }`/`@functions{ }`; classic ASP `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` `<% %>` and `<script language=\\\"JScript\\\" runat=\\\"server\\\">`; `[RunInstaller(true)]` Installer.Uninstall / `[ComRegisterFunction]`; Microsoft.Workflow.Compiler XOML `<x:Code><![CDATA[..]]>`; `csc.exe /out` invoked from batch with the source in an echo-redirected file. Extract each inner text (via nested-string-carrier-unescape), route to the language reader, report the host profile guess. Gate: D19 ASPX + D14 MSBuild + D8 php_webshell still route identically.\"},\n {\"id\":\"csharp-literal-fold\",\"concept\":\"static folding of assembled C#/.NET strings (descriptor built at runtime instead of a literal)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If a C#/VB.NET/F# variant assembles the descriptor: fold `string.Concat(..)`, `string.Join(\\\"\\\", new[] {..})`, `new string(new char[] {'v','=',..})`, `(char)0x76`/`(char)118`, `Encoding.UTF8|ASCII|Unicode.GetString(new byte[] {..})`, `Convert.FromBase64String`, `Convert.FromHexString`, `BitConverter`, `StringBuilder().Append(..)` chains, `$\\\"{a}{b}\\\"` over const locals, `.Reverse()`/`Array.Reverse`, `ToCharArray()` + `^ key` loops with literal keys, `\\\\u0076` escapes, verbatim/raw strings; VB `ChrW(118) & ..`, F# `String.concat \\\"\\\" [..]`. Pure regex/const-propagation over literals (no ast module, no compiler). Gate: D19 csx plans re-assembled in each form fold back to the same plan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fsharp-vbnet-script-route\",\"concept\":\"F# .fsx and VB.NET .vb / .vbx v=3 polyglots (next .NET languages)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Make sure the generic marker/descriptor readers cover: F# `// ` and `(* HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:.. *)` comments, `let descriptor_<id> = \\\"..\\\"`, triple-quoted `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `[<Literal>]` consts, `Map.ofList [ \\\"descriptor\\\", descriptor_<id> ]`; VB.NET `' HUNTRESS..` / `REM` comments, `Dim|Const descriptor_<id> As String = \\\"..\\\"` with `\\\"\\\"` escapes and `& _` line continuations, `New Dictionary(Of String, String) From {{\\\"descriptor\\\", ..}}`; JScript.NET `import System;` `var descriptor_<id> : String = \\\"..\\\"`. Family guesses `polyglot-fsharp_script` / `polyglot-vb_net` / `polyglot-jscript_net`. Gate: fixture battery of D19 plans in each syntax.\"},\n {\"id\":\"handoff-chain-resolve\",\"concept\":\"corpus-level handoff graph: where each bridge 'actually leads' (next_language -> member -> terminal)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 prompt 'resolve each static handoff and work out where the bridge actually leads' was answered by per-file next-language ids, but a corpus-level question (terminal language, chain length, which member a handoff resolves to, cycles, the file whose declared next_language disagrees with its code's spawn/write target) is the natural escalation. handoff_graph(plans_by_member, sources=None)->{edges: [(member, next_language, resolved_members)], chains, terminals, cycles, mismatches}; resolve next_language to members by plan language= / file family (`polyglot-<lang>-*`, host files, legacy v=1/v=2 names: jscript->.js, vbscript->.vbs, batch->.bat/.cmd, powershell->.ps1, python->.py, bash->.sh, node->.mjs); code-side target from declared_spawns/fetch_sites. handoff_answer(g, kind, accepted_values, what=). Reuse download_graph internals.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-script-host-route\",\"concept\":\"JSP webshell / Groovy / Java single-file / Nashorn hosts\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Sibling of D8 php_webshell and D19 aspx_inline_csharp on the JVM side: `<%@ page language=\\\"java\\\" import=..%>`, `<%-- HUNTRESS.. --%>` comments, scriptlets `<% %>`/declarations `<%! %>`, `Runtime.getRuntime().exec`/`ProcessBuilder`; Groovy `def descriptor_x = '..'` / `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `'''..'''`, `.execute()`, `.decodeBase64()`; Java `static final String DESCRIPTOR_X = \\\"..\\\";` with `\\\\uXXXX` escapes processed BEFORE lexing (unicode-escaped `\\\\u0022` can close a string or hide a comment end); Nashorn/Rhino `jrunscript -e`. Readers via nested-string-carrier-unescape; profile guesses `jsp_scriptlet`/`groovy_jenkins`. Gate: fixture battery.\"},\n]\nkeep=keep[:2]+new+keep[2:]\norder={'prebuild':0,'note':1,'tool':2}\nkeep.sort(key=lambda g:(g['priority'],order[g['action']]))\nprose=(\"Built by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16 night source-encoding-normalize, \"\n\"equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, \"\n\"yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route; D17 night download-graph-model, network-evidence-reconcile, plan-key-passthrough, \"\n\"indicator-refang-normalize, ahk-compiled-exe-extract, vba-module-route, dockerfile-makefile-route; D18 night network-evidence-indicators, \"\n\"source-fetch-sites, reconcile-indicator-kinds, http-redirect-dns-resolve, pcap-http-object-hashes, sysmon-proxy-log-fetches, \"\n\"ps-v3-polyglot-route, lolbin-download-attack-table, python-onion-regex-fold, v3-split-array-carrier, process-telemetry-windows, \"\n\"process-telemetry-linux-text, process-tree-model, static-process-tree, process-tree-reconcile, spawn-api-parent-table, cmdline-canon, \"\n\"saas-script-host-route (all `lib.codec`; earlier: batch-substring-emulation, container-carrier-extract, descriptor-syntax-generic, \"\n\"gzip-zlib-codec-rep, php-eval-chain, ps-layer-peel, v3-peel-widen, xslt-msxsl-route). Given up: python-exec-onion-static (2 attempts, \"\n\"`import ast` banned). Pending retries (1 failed attempt each): evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile. Prebuild gate: \"\n\"lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no csv/ast/tokenize/shlex/marshal; dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile OK). \"\n\"Priority-1 order for D20: the .NET/bridge thread D19 opened (nested-string-carrier-unescape -> managed-bridge-hosts -> \"\n\"dotnet-assembly-strings) plus the solver-side lib fallback note; then the second-evidence readers (router, file/registry) and the \"\n\"next .NET/JVM languages.\")\nbody=\"\\n\".join(json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in keep)\njs=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in keep)+\"\\n]\"\nt=t[:m.start()]+\"## Readiness gaps\\n\"+prose+\"\\n\\n```json\\n\"+js+\"\\n```\"+t[m.end():]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\ng2=json.loads(re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t,re.S).group(1))\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in g2 if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g2), 'pending prebuild', len(pend), pend)\nprint(all(set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for g in g2), len({g['id'] for g in g2})==len(g2))\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps prose and JSON queue"}}}
