{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBeakwnvDy2PipHe2fW4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both script-analysis files for day 19; I touched nothing else and ran no tests or GM modes.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/script-analysis.md`:**\n   - **Day 19 entry (\"Sharp Practice\").** The day added a Roslyn C# script (`.csx`, four polyglots) and an inline ASPX host, for 1249 ids in 137 members. The four polyglots were the usual plan-verbatim format. The twist was that the host file holds the whole inner script inside an escaped C# string (`\\n`, `\\\"`), so the carried solver left 11 ids with no plan.\n   - **What it cost.** The race harness put two guessed values into a 46-id bulk submit, which rejected the whole submit. Single solve was CORRECT at T+39 s with 2 wrong probes. `lib.codec.v3_plan` could already read that file; the solver just never called it.\n   - **Timed modes.** Time Trial took 5.3 s and Mastery (6245 ids) 12.2 s, both first try.\n   - **Other updates:**\n     - New variant axis for nested carriers, with the parse rule: unescape, rescan, and fall back to `lib.codec.v3_plan`.\n     - New recognition-cue rows for `.csx` and ASPX.\n     - New host profile `aspx_inline_csharp`.\n     - The ATT&CK question text itself says the parent technique (e.g. T1059) is accepted in place of a sub-technique, which explains why parent ids have worked all along.\n     - Pitfall: never put a guessed value in a bulk submit.\n   - I compressed the older day entries to make room. The file is 233 lines, a bit over the ~200 target.\n\n2. **`reference/coverage/script-analysis.md`:**\n   - Row 35 (C# script) and a new row 75 (server-side web-page hosts like ASPX) are marked `seen day19`.\n   - New gap rows: 76 (.NET assembly bytes inside a script) and 77 (JVM script hosts like JSP and Groovy).\n   - Updated rows: 34 (InstallUtil and similar, likelihood raised), 36 (F#/VB.NET) and 49 (carrier tags). Rows 71 and 72 now point to the process-tree functions already built in `lib.codec`.\n   - The recognition-cues block is exactly at the 60-line limit.\n\n3. **Readiness gaps.** The JSON block is still valid with the same keys and no reused ids.\n   - I dropped the 9 gaps that were built last night.\n   - Nine prebuild gaps are now pending (the floor is 8). Seven are new: `nested-string-carrier-unescape`, `managed-bridge-hosts` and `dotnet-assembly-strings` (all priority 1), plus `csharp-literal-fold`, `fsharp-vbnet-script-route`, `handoff-chain-resolve` and `jvm-script-host-route`. The other two are retries that failed once: `evidence-type-router` and `file-registry-telemetry-reconcile`.\n   - I also added a priority-1 note, `solver-lib-v3-fallback`: when the solver's own read finds no plan, it should call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":143513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":593},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d383f58c-515d-419c-8755-8a8284587d1d","uuid":"b5a38bb4-9564-4c09-a443-60781986518e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:08:51.086Z","request_id":"req_011CgBeakfvYKE4rVSRFE9rk"}
